4199898"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-99286" :question/id #uuid "ed6c8ff2-9373-55e7-924d-bdb8515b0668" :question/math-academy-id "q-99286" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨2{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each componentt separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨2{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(2{e}^{t}){|}_{0}^{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{|}_{0}^{1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{1}-2{e}^{0},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2e-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-99286/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-99286"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123435/selection/e6c787b5675364dfe01b858415acce4ef776f727dbf353ce24887787dafe1cc6" :answer/id #uuid "643d4235-fe2a-5067-8e7c-c1c81d3bc507" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123435/selection/c2e3082514d6e05a504a1d8e637de5277442cbc29eb11eefe2df99c53a062f3d" :answer/id #uuid "302d4f57-97ec-54bb-b2e7-cb1539f6f5f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123435/selection/880a717dea3c7ad687e3f36fea4666dcc492ae41464eff593cb260d47353dcd0" :answer/id #uuid "4aeedef3-75c1-5ba0-b55f-0580f364c910" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{e}^{3t},\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123435/selection/d0cbf6232171ad301056006765d3d79640df521a40f550ee2966be5b27abd801" :answer/id #uuid "e3aa1818-e4e7-5c6f-97c0-c202791b7d7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t-1},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123435/selection/53d5ef093994b9cb1fb3df82e3b663667621b75dbbb4afa445f1275e1f06ddd7" :answer/id #uuid "21d81a6a-c181-537d-a961-fa8020325bc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123435/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "748165c9-e9ef-5229-8cc7-2d5dc972ce8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123435/selection/53d5ef093994b9cb1fb3df82e3b663667621b75dbbb4afa445f1275e1f06ddd7" :answer-field/choices ["q-123435/selection/e6c787b5675364dfe01b858415acce4ef776f727dbf353ce24887787dafe1cc6" "q-123435/selection/c2e3082514d6e05a504a1d8e637de5277442cbc29eb11eefe2df99c53a062f3d" "q-123435/selection/880a717dea3c7ad687e3f36fea4666dcc492ae41464eff593cb260d47353dcd0" "q-123435/selection/d0cbf6232171ad301056006765d3d79640df521a40f550ee2966be5b27abd801" "q-123435/selection/53d5ef093994b9cb1fb3df82e3b663667621b75dbbb4afa445f1275e1f06ddd7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123435" :question/id #uuid "ae9740d6-44f0-50b4-8094-5aec220611bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-123435" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)⟩\\text{d}t=⟨\\int {e}^{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t)={e}^{t+1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t+1}\\text{d}t={e}^{t+1}+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u=3t.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 12\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)+{c}_{2} \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{e}^{t+1}+{c}_{1},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123435/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123435"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123438/selection/cb19c38f82245b79e9f1dfd6739c8bee8d79a74a6e81ca8b02e8513525455feb" :answer/id #uuid "a97f4408-8e22-58c3-82e8-cb54939afe47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123438/selection/ddfed34112fcbf546e1cb5194b387bc70bbb776c7ca1282df037b7f19fa65632" :answer/id #uuid "b186173f-82e8-521f-aec7-439a4de5e036" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123438/selection/49665e93751959e27e96c23508794df9c02d5929b2b211aea0d4c699d7ce8f9a" :answer/id #uuid "d4e371f2-60bb-58cd-a297-df8554ebd10f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123438/selection/7b3ce8e2bbe2aa51f904e54cb61ba812ac51f6e0519a80802345860c44c7226f" :answer/id #uuid "afc924f9-d777-5b34-8376-c280a6938f86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t),\\,(t-1){e}^{t-1}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123438/selection/a5ab2f1a57177976bda1758bbc2d323812f880e159ecbabc52e986d2e77e9101" :answer/id #uuid "5acbc104-ce25-5e12-8606-3bd2bdf673b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123438/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "34631f09-fd89-5a00-996a-25cf1cee1140" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123438/selection/ddfed34112fcbf546e1cb5194b387bc70bbb776c7ca1282df037b7f19fa65632" :answer-field/choices ["q-123438/selection/cb19c38f82245b79e9f1dfd6739c8bee8d79a74a6e81ca8b02e8513525455feb" "q-123438/selection/ddfed34112fcbf546e1cb5194b387bc70bbb776c7ca1282df037b7f19fa65632" "q-123438/selection/49665e93751959e27e96c23508794df9c02d5929b2b211aea0d4c699d7ce8f9a" "q-123438/selection/7b3ce8e2bbe2aa51f904e54cb61ba812ac51f6e0519a80802345860c44c7226f" "q-123438/selection/a5ab2f1a57177976bda1758bbc2d323812f880e159ecbabc52e986d2e77e9101"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123438" :question/id #uuid "53bd3a98-c5a9-50e2-9a0c-9c6d9fc4a3f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-123438" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩\\text{d}t=⟨\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4})\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int {e}^{t-1}\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u=\\frac{t}{4}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}t=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot 4\\text{d}u \\\\  & =8\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =8(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)+{c}_{1} \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4})+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)={e}^{t-1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t-1}\\text{d}t={e}^{t-1}+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4})+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{t-1}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{4}),\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123438/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123438"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-349111/field-1/a9c8c203bec6e9eb753286828ae45b1c5b78232955f3a3480ea7cfd3cfc53df7" :answer/id #uuid "ef4b79f6-2a0e-56e7-a3dc-cf08da2ed808" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(\\frac{4}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349111/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d3c18101-7b84-5d9f-87ea-61425edb9ffc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349111/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "27743efa-ff2c-511b-8c8f-a70142bb6cbf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349111/field-1/a9c8c203bec6e9eb753286828ae45b1c5b78232955f3a3480ea7cfd3cfc53df7" :answer-field/choices ["q-349111/field-1/a9c8c203bec6e9eb753286828ae45b1c5b78232955f3a3480ea7cfd3cfc53df7" "q-349111/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349111/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "2e371808-48dc-57ca-a575-08e8b286b602" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349111/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a03a3b8-178b-5974-9fa8-b8781e810cd6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349111/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-349111/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349111" :question/id #uuid "eda8ba15-b3ac-5012-8eb1-39f51ec5e92c" :question/math-academy-id "q-349111" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral of a vector-valued function. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}⟨\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t}{2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t},\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}⟨\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t}{2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t},\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t}{2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component, let $u=2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$, so $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t}{2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second component, we integrate directly:\n\n$$\n\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}⟨\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t}{2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t},\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t){|}_{0}^{\\pi /3},\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3),\\,-4\\,(\\frac{1}{2}-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨ln\\,(\\frac{4}{3}),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨ln\\,(\\frac{4}{3}),\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-349111/field-1" "q-349111/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-349111"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-349375/field-1/6d903bfa835a59a5a5eb375db6af61996ead5c2fa3c9788be894285a78f8db6c" :answer/id #uuid "3162d22b-0690-5157-8a6d-c0205a3b2f7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2e^{-t}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349375/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "07d9e588-62c4-59f4-8664-77763004fe06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349375/field-1/6d903bfa835a59a5a5eb375db6af61996ead5c2fa3c9788be894285a78f8db6c" :answer-field/choices ["q-349375/field-1/6d903bfa835a59a5a5eb375db6af61996ead5c2fa3c9788be894285a78f8db6c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349375/field-2/d51cbc0ba94c4b0f63c4e5dd78e5348792b714cc47e647b4f0331f19bc839794" :answer/id #uuid "7b9df6a5-a988-5c39-bad5-001540f474a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t^3-2t-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349375/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7af77894-a863-5f95-88d1-caf0b8d43662" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349375/field-2/d51cbc0ba94c4b0f63c4e5dd78e5348792b714cc47e647b4f0331f19bc839794" :answer-field/choices ["q-349375/field-2/d51cbc0ba94c4b0f63c4e5dd78e5348792b714cc47e647b4f0331f19bc839794"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349375" :question/id #uuid "2e9e3108-2328-5f57-9874-50475f372469" :question/math-academy-id "q-349375" :question/problem "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=⟨2{e}^{-t}\\,,6{t}^{2}-2⟩\n$$\n\n and $F(0)=⟨1,\\,-4⟩.$\n\n$F(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨2{e}^{-t}\\,,6{t}^{2}-2⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨2{e}^{-t}\\,,6{t}^{2}-2⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 2{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 6{t}^{2}-2\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{e}^{-t}+{c}_{1},\\,2{t}^{3}-2t+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(0)=⟨1,\\,-4⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨-2{e}^{0}+{c}_{1},\\,2(0)^{3}-2(0)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,-4⟩ \\\\ ⟨-2+{c}_{1},\\,0+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=3$ and ${c}_{2}=-4.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨-2{e}^{-t}+3,\\,2{t}^{3}-2t-4⟩.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-349375/field-1" "q-349375/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-349375"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
